RISC-V: drop shift-count masks the shift instructions already apply. Applied after perf-43; JIT only.
- sll/srl/sra read the low 6 bits of the count and sllw/srlw/sraw the low 5, the same masking the IR's
  shift semantics assume (gtFoldExprConst and VN mask the count too). Lowering's TryRemoveShiftRotateMask
  removes such an AND only while it is still the shift's direct operand; C# emits "& 63" at every long
  shift, so a count shared by several shifts is CSE'd with its mask into a local and keeps an andi (and
  often a callee-saved register) per use. Global morph now drops an AND whose constant keeps every count
  bit before CSE runs (an over-mask such as "& 15" stays).
- Lowering also drops an ADD/SUB of a multiple of the width from the count: "x >> ((64 - s) & 63)" becomes
  "x >> -s" (negw instead of negw + addiw). Rotate recognition in morph still sees "-y + N".
- VN's folding of a 32-bit shift by a constant now masks the count with 0x1F, as gtFoldExprConst does; a
  count that used to arrive masked can now be propagated to it as a constant of 32 or more.

--- a/src/coreclr/jit/lower.cpp
+++ b/src/coreclr/jit/lower.cpp
@@ -8977,6 +8977,27 @@
         // The parent was replaced, clear contain and regOpt flag.
         op->gtOp2->ClearContained();
     }
+
+#ifdef TARGET_RISCV64
+    // Adding or subtracting a multiple of the width leaves the count bits alone: "x >> ((-y + 64) & 63)" needs
+    // only the negation.
+    while (op->gtGetOp2()->OperIs(GT_ADD, GT_SUB) && !op->gtGetOp2()->gtOverflow())
+    {
+        GenTree* addOp  = op->gtGetOp2();
+        GenTree* addend = addOp->gtGetOp2();
+
+        if (!addend->IsCnsIntOrI() || addend->AsIntCon()->ImmedValNeedsReloc(m_compiler) ||
+            ((static_cast<size_t>(addend->AsIntCon()->IconValue()) & mask) != 0))
+        {
+            break;
+        }
+
+        op->gtOp2 = addOp->gtGetOp1();
+        BlockRange().Remove(addOp);
+        BlockRange().Remove(addend);
+        op->gtOp2->ClearContained();
+    }
+#endif
 }
 
